{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race data or evaluator feedback, so this is a conservative first candidate built from the contract. Geometry: five line sensors spread across the body at x = +0.03, +0.015, 0, -0.015, -0.03 m and y = 0.05 m (ahead of the axle), so the line is seen before the wheels reach it. The 0.012 m footprint is smaller than the 0.025 m tape, so the sensors can resolve the line edge. A 0.12 m wheel track, 0.03 m wheel radius, 0.8 kg mass and 0.16 x 0.12 m body are mid-range values that keep yaw inertia moderate and the off-track limit at 0.06 m. Controller: weights are proportional to sensor x (2, 1, 0, -1, -2), so signal is about offset/0.015 m in the linear region, with |signal| up to 2 at the outer sensors. kp = 3 gives roughly 70,000 PWM per metre of offset, a firm but not saturating correction for a 1 cm error. ki = 0 avoids integral windup on the curves. kd = 0.1 damps the turn-in oscillation without amplifying sensor noise much. base_speed = 1.7 gives about 85 percent of full PWM, aiming for the roughly 1.5 m/s average needed to finish in 3 s while leaving headroom for slower bends. line_loss = last_direction keeps the robot turning toward the side it last saw the line. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with rms_error well under 0.03 m. The slalom may show oscillation or line loss at the faster speed. Hypotheses to test: (1) speed is limited by the bends rather than by the motors; (2) kp = 3 is near the oscillation boundary, so steering_oscillation will tell us whether to lower it or add kd; (3) the 0.012 m sensors give enough overlap for a clean signal at the outer weights. Measurements requested: all metrics, so the evaluator and next iteration can see completion time against the 3 s limit, line-loss events, and jitter.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": 0.03, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.015, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.015, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.03, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.7,
    "kp": 3.0,
    "ki": 0.0,
    "kd": 0.1,
    "sensor_weights": [2.0, 1.0, 0.0, -1.0, -2.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "controller_errors",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "First candidate: five 12 mm sensors at 3 cm spacing, kp=3, kd=0.1, base_speed=1.7, last_direction line-loss. No race data yet, so values follow the contract's mid-range and the sensor-to-signal geometry. The next iteration should adjust kp, kd and speed from the oscillation and completion-time results."
    }
  }
}
